'To set a password item to not save state, edit the item by clicking on the <strong>Item Name</strong> and ',
'set the <strong>Session State, Storage</strong> attribute to <strong>Per Request (Memory Only)</strong>.</p>',
'',
'<p>When password items require session state to be maintained between page views, ',
'Oracle recommends encrypting the item values. To encrypt item session state, edit ',
'the item and enable the <strong>Security, Store value encrypted in session state</strong> ',
'attribute.</p>',
'',
'<p>Oracle also recommends disabling HTML form auto completion on pages with ',
'passwords. To disable auto completion, edit the page attributes and set the ',
'<strong>Security, Form Auto Complete</strong> value to <strong>Off</strong>.</p>',
'',
'<p>At risk password items, are password items that save state and are not ',
'encrypted.</p>'))
