wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_item(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1403940863419758219)
,p_name=>'P179_RESET_GRID'
,p_item_sequence=>50
,p_item_plug_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(57540512543180628)
,p_item_default=>'ALL'
,p_display_as=>'NATIVE_HIDDEN'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>When switching from one theme to another theme you have the option to reset the region and item grid settings. The grid settings define the positioning of your regions and items on a page. Regions might be positioned next to each other or you migh'
||'t have a form that has two or more items in a single row. Resetting the grid will remove these settings and render all regions and items stacked up vertically. </p>',
'',
'<p>When switching from a theme using a table-based grid, such as Theme 26 (Productivity Applications), to a theme using a DIV-based grid, like Theme 42 (Universal Theme) any regions that have a fixed position need to be reset, i.e. the "Reset fixed r'
||'egion positions" option needs to be selected.  </p>',
'',
'<p>When switching from one theme to another theme, where both themes use the same grid type, no reset is required, and the "Keep current region and item grid settings" option can be selected.</p>',
'',
'<p>It is also possible to reset the grid for all regions and items. This is useful when switching from an old theme to a newer, DIV-based theme in order to prepare for re-doing the page and form layout for all pages. Please note that all previous reg'
||'ion and item position settings will be lost when choosing this option.</p>',
''))
,p_encrypt_session_state_yn=>'N'
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'value_protected', 'Y')).to_clob
);
