wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1447696670584402)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event install'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>130
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The install event of the service worker interface is fired as soon as the worker executes, and it''s only called once per service worker.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to populate a cache with a number of resources, which the service worker can then use to serve assets.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/install_event">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/install_event</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/primers/service-workers/lifecycle#install">https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/primers/service-workers/lifecycle#install</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1448731379584413)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event activate'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>140
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The activate event of the service worker interface is fired when your service worker is ready to control clients and handle functional events like push and sync.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to update or clean existing caches.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/activate_event">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/activate_event</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/primers/service-workers/lifecycle#activate">https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/primers/service-workers/lifecycle#activate</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1448825540584414)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event push'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>170
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The push event of the service worker interface is fired when a push message has been received. It contains the information sent from an application server to a push subcriber.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to display a notification on a device controlled by the service worker.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications">https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/PushEvent">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/PushEvent</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1448945715584415)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event notificationclick'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>190
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The notificationclick event of the service worker interface is fired when client clicks on a notification sent by the service worker.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to trigger actions or open pages when clicking a notification.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications#the_notificationclick_event">https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications#the_notificationclick_ev'
||'ent</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/notificationclick_event">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/notificationclick_event</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449046848584416)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event fetch'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>150
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The fetch event of the service worker interface is fired when a request is made from the client.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to determine what to do with the request before sending the request to a server. For example, the service worker can look for resources in the cache and serve those resources instead. Implementations of the fetch event can lead to f'
||'aster page loads and offline capabilities.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API/Using_Service_Workers">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API/Using_Service_Workers</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449136594584417)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event sync'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>160
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The sync event of the service worker interface is fired when network connectivity comes available after being unavailable.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to send requests to the server that were unable to proceed when the client was offline.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/sync_event">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/sync_event</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/updates/2015/12/background-sync">https://developers.google.com/web/updates/2015/12/background-sync</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449244061584418)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event canmakepayment'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>210
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The canmakepayment event of the service worker interface is fired when the client requests the authorization status of the Payment Handler API.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to check if the browser supports at least one payment method.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Payment_Request_API/Using_the_Payment_Request_API">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Payment_Request_API/Using_the_Payment_Request_API</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://web.dev/web-payments-updates">https://web.dev/web-payments-updates</a>/</li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-handler/#handling-a-canmakepaymentevent">https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-handler/#handling-a-canmakepaymentevent</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449367005584419)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event notificationclose'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>200
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The notificationclose event of the service worker interface is fired when a user dismisses a notification, such as a swipe on a mobile device.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to log the event to your analytics database, or log the event to avoid re-notifying the user of the same event.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications#the_notificationclose_event">https://developers.google.com/web/ilt/pwa/introduction-to-push-notifications#the_notificationclose_ev'
||'ent</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449497849584420)
,p_plug_name=>'Help - Event paymentrequest'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:js-dialog-size480x320'
,p_plug_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(557449278618308550)
,p_plug_display_sequence=>220
,p_plug_display_point=>'REGION_POSITION_03'
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>The paymentrequest event of the service worker interface is fired when client chooses to pay with a web-based payment app.</p>',
'<p>It can be used to initiate a payment on a web app, using payment methods such as Google Pay.</p>',
'<p>More info:</p>',
'<ul>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://web.dev/how-payment-request-api-works/">https://web.dev/how-payment-request-api-works/</a></li>',
'    <li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://web.dev/orchestrating-payment-transactions/">https://web.dev/orchestrating-payment-transactions/</a></li>',
'</ul>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
