wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_item(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(5568492123228162)
,p_name=>'P1117_OPTIMIZER_HINT'
,p_source_data_type=>'VARCHAR2'
,p_item_sequence=>10
,p_item_plug_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(4033026375134831)
,p_item_source_plug_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3607047868896004)
,p_prompt=>'Optimizer Hint'
,p_source=>'OPTIMIZER_HINT'
,p_source_type=>'REGION_SOURCE_COLUMN'
,p_display_as=>'NATIVE_TEXT_FIELD'
,p_cSize=>60
,p_cMaxlength=>255
,p_field_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(561547836135222071)
,p_item_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_is_persistent=>'N'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter the Oracle Optimizer hint which is added to the top-level statement when executing the SQL query. A hint is an instruction to the Optimizer. When writing SQL, you may know information about the data unknown to the Optimizer. Hints enable you'
||' to make decisions normally made by the Optimizer, sometimes causing the Optimizer to select a plan that it sees as higher cost.</p>',
'',
'<p>For example, you might know that a certain index is more selective for certain queries. Based on this information, you might be able to choose a more efficient execution plan than the Optimizer. In such a case, use hints to force the Optimizer to '
||'use the optimal execution plan.</p>',
'',
'<p>Example:</p>',
'<p>When accessing the table <code>employees</code>, try to use the index <code>emp_department_ix</code>:</p>',
'<pre>INDEX (employees emp_department_ix)</pre>'))
,p_encrypt_session_state_yn=>'N'
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'disabled', 'N',
  'send_on_page_submit', 'N',
  'submit_when_enter_pressed', 'N',
  'subtype', 'TEXT',
  'trim_spaces', 'BOTH')).to_clob
);
