'<p>',
'    Choose the data type of the parameter value. When a non-VARCHAR2 value ',
'    is sent to the REST API, it will be converted to a string using the ',
'    <strong>Output Format Mask</strong>.',
'</p>',
'<p>Options include</p>',
'<dl>',
'    <dt>String</dt>',
'    <dd>String values contain alphanumeric data.</dt>',
'    <dt>Numeric</dt>',
'    <dd>Numeric values are decimal or integer values.</dd>',
'    <dt>Date</dt>',
'    <dd>Date values contain date and time, but neither fractional seconds nor time zone information.</dd>',
'    <dt>Timestamp</dt>',
'    <dd>Timestamp values contain date and time (including fractional seconds), but no time zone information.</dd>',
'    <dt>Timestamp with Time Zone</dt>',
'    <dd>Timestamp with Time Zone values contain date and time (including fractional seconds), as well as time zone information.</dd>',
'    <dt>Boolean</dt>',
'    <dd>Boolean values contain <strong>true</strong> or <strong>false</strong>.</dd>',
'    <dt>Binary</dt>',
'    <dd>Binary content contains non-text (image, raw bytes) data, and are represented as a String in <em>Base64</em> format.</dd>',
'</dl>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
