'    <li><strong>Data</strong> column values are directly extracted from the source data (uploaded data or REST Source response). A <strong>Data</strong> column always requires the <strong>Selector</strong> attribute to be set.</li>',
'    <li><strong>Lookup</strong> columns are used to "look up" a value from a table, based on (another) <strong>Data</strong> column. For instance, a lookup can be defined to return the <strong>DEPTNO</strong> value from the <strong>DEPT</strong> tabl'
||'e, based on the value of the <strong>DNAME</strong> Data Column.',
'    </li>',
'    <li><strong>SQL Expression</strong> columns compute a value based on other <strong>Data Columns</strong> using a SQL Expression.</li>',
'    <li><strong>SQL Query</strong> columns will execute a SQL query, which references other <strong>Data Columns</strong> in order to retrieve a value.</li>',
'</ul> '))
);
