,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter the name of the PL/SQL function to be called to release locked resources or cancel associated rows within a workflow context, especially when a plug-in implements a wait state. ',
'By invoking the terminate function, the plugin can effectively free up resources if the associated workflow instance gets terminated.',
'It can reference a function of the anonymous PL/SQL code block, a package function or stand alone function in the database. For example:',
'<pre>',
'terminate_proc',
'</pre></p>',
'',
'<p>When referencing a database PL/SQL package or stand alone function, you can use the <code>#OWNER#</code> substitution string to reference the parsing schema of the current application. For example:',
'<pre>',
'#OWNER#.terminate_proc',
'</pre></p>',
'',
'<p>Process Type Plug-in Termination Functions must implement the following interface:',
'',
'<pre>',
'function name_of_function (',
'    p_process in apex_plugin.t_process,',
'    p_plugin  in apex_plugin.t_plugin )',
'    return apex_plugin.t_process_terminate_result',
'',
'</pre>',
'</p>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
