wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_item(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3702247340120801)
,p_name=>'P7022_EMAIL_BODY_HTML'
,p_item_sequence=>130
,p_item_plug_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1936683460374337)
,p_prompt=>'Body HTML'
,p_display_as=>'PLUGIN_COM.ORACLE.APEX.CODE_EDITOR'
,p_cSize=>30
,p_cMaxlength=>4000
,p_cHeight=>8
,p_field_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(561547836135222071)
,p_item_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter text that yields a multi-part HTML message, including both plain text and HTML content. The settings and capabilities of the recipient&#39;s email client will determine what displays. Although most modern email clients can read an HTML forma'
||'tted email, remember that some users disable this functionality to address security issues. Use substitution syntax, such as <code>&amp;P6_PRODUCT_NAME.</code>, if you want to include dynamic content in the text.</p>',
'<p>When referencing images using the &lt;img /&gt; tag, remember that the images must be accessible to the recipient&#39;s email client in order for them to see the image. For example, suppose you reference an image on your network called hello.gif a'
||'s follows:</p>',
'<pre>',
'&lt;img src=&quot;http://example.com/hello.gif&quot; alt=&quot;Hello&quot; /&gt;',
'</pre>',
'<p>In this example, the image is not attached to the email, but is referenced by the email. For the recipient to see it, they must be able to access the image using a Web browser. If the image is inside a firewall and the recipient is outside of the '
||'firewall, the image will not display. For this reason, avoid using images. If you must include images, be sure to include the ALT attribute to provide a textual description in the event the image is not accessible.</p>',
'<p><em>Note: The SMTP/MIME specification dictates that no single line shall exceed 1000 characters. To comply with this restriction, you must add a carriage return or line feed characters to break your text into chunks of 1000 characters or less. Fai'
||'ling to do so will result in erroneous email messages, including partial messages or messages with extraneous exclamation points.</em></p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'attribute_01', 'HTMLMIXED',
  'attribute_02', 'VARCHAR2',
  'attribute_03', 'Y',
  'attribute_04', 'N',
  'attribute_07', 'N')).to_clob
);
wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_item(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3702317872120802)
,p_name=>'P7022_EMAIL_ATTACH_QUERY'
,p_item_sequence=>140
,p_item_plug_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1936683460374337)
,p_prompt=>'Attachment SQL'
,p_display_as=>'PLUGIN_COM.ORACLE.APEX.CODE_EDITOR'
,p_cSize=>65
,p_cMaxlength=>4000
,p_cHeight=>5
,p_field_template=>wwv_flow_imp.id(561547836135222071)
,p_item_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter a SQL statement which returns one or more BLOBs that are attached as files to the e-mail.</p>',
'<p>If the content_id column contains a null value then the associated files will be regular attachments. Files such as documents or zip archives are generally attached in this way.</p>',
'<p>If the value of the content_id is non-null then the associated file will be marked as being attached inline. The value of the content_id column will be used as the CID (Content ID) of the attachment. This CID value can be used in the HTML code of '
||'the email in order to embed images directly within the email content. Note that some email clients may not automatically display inline attachments. Also note that email standards dictate various requirements for the format of content identifiers. Or'
||'acle &PRODUCT_NAME. does not enforce compliance with these standards.</p>',
'<p></p>',
'<p>The SQL statement must be in the following format:</p>',
'<pre>',
'select blob_column,',
'       file_name,',
'       mime_type,',
'       content_id',
'  from table',
'</pre>',
'<p>The columns mime_type and content_id are optional. If content_id is present then the file will be attached inline and the value of content_id will be used for the attachment''s CID.</p>',
'<p>If the content_id column contains the value ''my_inline_content'' then that image may be embedded within the email using the following HTML:</p>',
'<p>',
'<pre>',
'&lt;div&gt;',
'&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;h1&gt;Some Embedded Content&lt;/h1&gt;',
'&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;p&gt;',
'&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;img src="cid:my_inline_content" alt="Inline Image" &gt;',
'&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;',
'&lt;/div&gt;',
'</pre>',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'attribute_01', 'SQL',
  'attribute_02', 'VARCHAR2',
  'attribute_03', 'N',
  'attribute_04', 'N',
  'attribute_07', 'N')).to_clob
);
